## Overview

Petalnex delivers custom software, AI, and automation solutions to clients on an ongoing project basis. Once a solution is deployed, clients need a reliable channel to report issues, request changes, or check on progress — but handling these requests manually makes it hard to triage urgency, track resolution status, or maintain a consistent record of what was asked and how it was resolved.

This project automates the intake and triage of that pipeline:

**Inquiry intake → validation → AI classification & sentiment → priority detection → [knowledge-base search] → [human review] → ticket storage → [notifications]**

Stages in brackets are designed and documented but not yet built — see [Remaining Work](#remaining-work).

## Architecture

![Architecture Diagram](./docs/CustomerSupport-Architecture-Diagram.png)

Seven stages carry a ticket from submission to a recorded, human-reviewed outcome. Teal stages are AI-driven; every other stage is deterministic.

Full breakdown of components, integrations, and design rationale: [`docs/CustomerSupport-Component-Credentials-List.docx`](./docs/CustomerSupport-Component-Credentials-List.docx)

## Technologies

| Layer | Technology | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Orchestration | [n8n](https://n8n.io) (self-hosted) | Form Trigger, Code, If, Postgres nodes |
| AI / LLM | Google Gemini | Classification, sentiment analysis; embeddings planned for RAG |
| Data storage | Supabase (Postgres) | Ticket records, classification, priority, full audit trail |
| Notifications | Gmail SMTP | Planned: client acknowledgement + internal team routing |

